  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A circle cuts a chord of length 4 a on the $x$ -axis and passes through a point on the $y$ -axis, distant $2 \\mathrm{~b}$ from the origin. Then the locus of the centre of this circle, is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "AXkWC",
      "text": "a hyperbola",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ttL9A",
      "text": "an ellipse",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dVKU6",
      "text": "a straight line",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gB2eC",
      "text": "a parabola",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/jcChSBnovtRTzVISRP-iGRFAGiX9hts05s5_-2erfPM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nLet centre be $C(h, k)$\r\n\r\n$C Q=C P=r$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow C Q^{2}=C P^{2}$\r\n\r\n$(h-0)^{2}+(k \\pm 0)^{2}=C M^{2}+M P^{2}$\r\n\r\n$h^{2}+(k \\pm 2 \\mathrm{~b})^{2}=k^{2}+4 a^{2}$\r\n\r\n$h^{2}+k^{2}+4 b^{2} \\pm 4 b k=k^{2}+4 a^{2}$\r\n\r\nThen, the locus of centre $C(h, k)$\r\n\r\n$x^{2}+4 b^{2} \\pm 4 b y=4 a^{2}$\r\n\r\nHence, the above locus of the centre of circle is a\r\n\r\nparabola.",
